</section>

<h3 id="screen-reader-quirks" class="@GlobalValues.Info_Box_Heading_Class">Screen reader quirks or known issues</h3>
<ul aria-labelledby="screen-reader-quirks">
    <li>
        <b>Narrator</b> more often than not will not announce that the accordion item has been expanded after clicking the heading when
        paried with either Edge or Chrome, but is fine when paired with Firefox.
    </li>
    <li>
        <b>NVDA</b> on all browsers. When in Browse mode on clicking a collapsed accordion header it will announce that its expanded, twice.
        In Focus mode it works as expected.
    </li>
    <li>
        <b>JAWS</b> paired with Firefox will sometimes repeat accordion heading names and actions, expanded/collapsed.
    </li>
    <li>
        <b>VoiceOver</b> on the macOS paired with Safari seems to stutter on expanding accordion items.
    </li>
</ul>


<section>
    <h2 class="page-heading">Installation</h2>

    <p>
        <strong>Note: </strong> It is a requirement that the Blazor Ramp Core <span class="code-span">core-live-region.js</span> script, <span class="code-span">LiveRegionService</span>, and
        associated <span class="code-span">&lt;AnnouncementHistory /&gt;</span> component are added alongside this component’s specific
        requirements (a stylesheet reference in this instance). You do not need to add the BlazorRamp.Core package separately, as BlazorRamp.Core is included as a transitive package, you only need to add the packages that contain the components
        that you wish to use i.e the <b>BlazorRamp.Tabs</b> NuGet package.
    </p>
    <p>
        Please follow the instructions in the <a class="@GlobalValues.Link_Class" href="@GlobalValues.Path_Overview_Getting_Started">@GlobalValues.Main_Nav_Section_Heading_About - @GlobalValues.Page_Heading_Overview_Getting_Started</a>
        ensuring that in the <span class="code-span">&lt;head&gt;</span> section you also add the Tabs stylesheet as follows:
    </p>
    <CodeBox CodeBlock="@CodeSnippets.Add_Accordion_Style_Sheet" AriaLabel="Add Accordion stylesheet code block" />

</section>

<section class="code-table">

    <h2 id="accordion-component-parameters" class="code-table__heading">Accordion component (parent) parameters</h2>

    <table aria-labelledby="accordion-component-parameters">

        <thead>
            <tr>
                <th scope="col">Parameter</th>
                <th scope="col">Type</th>
                <th scope="col">Description</th>
            </tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
            <tr>
                <td>ChildContent</td>
                <td>RenderFragment?</td>
                <td>
                    The render fragment used for the child content (for each AccordionItem).
                </td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
                <td>ExpandMode</td>
                <td>ExpandMode (enum)?</td>
                <td>
                    Determines where there can be one <span class="code-span">ExpandMode.Single</span> or 
                    multiple  <span class="code-span">ExpandMode.Multiple</span> panels open at once. 
                    Defaults to <span class="code-span">ExpandMode.Multiple</span>.
                </td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
                <td>OnAccordionItemHeadingClicked</td>
                <td>EventCallback&lt;ItemHeadingData&gt;</td>
                <td>
                    Event raised when a heading is clicked providing information such
                    the index and name of the heading clicked and whether its collapsed or expanded. 
                </td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
                <td>AdditionalAttributes</td>
                <td>Dictionary&lt;string, object&gt;?</td>
                <td>Sets additional attributes applied to the component's root element.</td>
            </tr>
        </tbody>
    </table>
